    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Thanks, that's a good start. For the 'Urban' one, it's still feeling a little bit 'corporate trying to be cool.' If we're really targeting those inner-city demographics to build genuine rapport, shouldn't the language be a bit more authentic to how people actually talk in those neighborhoods? \n\nMaybe lean more into some local slang or a more relaxed dialect so it doesn't feel like a script. Can you give me a version that feels less 'standard casual' and more like it's actually coming from someone in that community? Like, more 'street' or authentic to an urban environment?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
